adjudication.rationale:
In `sendAddGuestsEmails(calEvent, newGuests)`, the code unconditionally iterates over `calendarEvent.attendees` and sends an email to *each* attendee on every invocation:
```ts
emailsToSend.push(
  ...calendarEvent.attendees.map((attendee) => {
    if (newGuests.includes(attendee.email)) {
      return sendEmail(() => new AttendeeScheduledEmail(calendarEvent, attendee));
    } else {
      return sendEmail(() => new AttendeeAddGuestsEmail(calendarEvent, attendee));
    }
  })
);
```
Since `evt.attendees` is built from `bookingAttendees.attendees` (which includes all existing + newly added attendees after the DB update), every call sends mail to the whole attendee list, not just the newly added guests. As guests are added in multiple operations, the number of emails sent per operation grows with current attendee count, producing quadratic total volume across sequential additions and re-notifying existing attendees about unrelated additions.
